{"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/OUDSTokensSemantic\/documentation\/OUDSTokensSemantic\/MultipleElevationCompositeRawToken"},"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"kind":"symbol","sections":[],"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Class","title":"MultipleElevationCompositeRawToken","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MultipleElevationCompositeRawToken","kind":"identifier"}],"symbolKind":"class","modules":[{"name":"Tokens for semantics"}],"role":"symbol","platforms":[{"beta":false,"introducedAt":"15.0","deprecated":false,"name":"iOS","unavailable":false},{"beta":false,"introducedAt":"15.0","deprecated":false,"name":"iPadOS","unavailable":false},{"beta":false,"introducedAt":"15.0","deprecated":false,"name":"Mac Catalyst","unavailable":false},{"beta":false,"introducedAt":"13.0","deprecated":false,"name":"macOS","unavailable":false},{"beta":false,"introducedAt":"16.0","deprecated":false,"name":"tvOS","unavailable":false},{"beta":false,"introducedAt":"1.0","deprecated":false,"name":"visionOS","unavailable":false},{"beta":false,"introducedAt":"11.0","deprecated":false,"name":"watchOS","unavailable":false}],"fragments":[{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MultipleElevationCompositeRawToken","kind":"identifier"}],"externalID":"c:@M@OUDSTokensSemantic@objc(cs)MultipleElevationCompositeRawToken"},"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/OUDSTokensSemantic\/documentation\/OUDSTokensSemantic\/MultipleElevationCompositeRawToken\/init(_:)","doc:\/\/OUDSTokensSemantic\/documentation\/OUDSTokensSemantic\/MultipleElevationCompositeRawToken\/init(light:dark:)"],"anchor":"Initializers","title":"Initializers","generated":true},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/OUDSTokensSemantic\/documentation\/OUDSTokensSemantic\/MultipleElevationCompositeRawToken\/dark","doc:\/\/OUDSTokensSemantic\/documentation\/OUDSTokensSemantic\/MultipleElevationCompositeRawToken\/light"],"anchor":"Instance-Properties","title":"Instance Properties","generated":true},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/OUDSTokensSemantic\/documentation\/OUDSTokensSemantic\/MultipleElevationCompositeRawToken\/elevation(for:)","doc:\/\/OUDSTokensSemantic\/documentation\/OUDSTokensSemantic\/MultipleElevationCompositeRawToken\/isEqual(_:)"],"anchor":"Instance-Methods","title":"Instance Methods","generated":true}],"relationshipsSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/OUDSTokensSemantic\/objc(cs)NSObject"],"title":"Inherits From","kind":"relationships","type":"inheritsFrom"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/OUDSTokensSemantic\/objc(pl)NSObject","doc:\/\/OUDSTokensSemantic\/s7CVarArgP","doc:\/\/OUDSTokensSemantic\/s28CustomDebugStringConvertibleP","doc:\/\/OUDSTokensSemantic\/s23CustomStringConvertibleP","doc:\/\/OUDSTokensSemantic\/SQ","doc:\/\/OUDSTokensSemantic\/SH","doc:\/\/OUDSTokensSemantic\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/OUDSTokensSemantic\/s16SendableMetatypeP"],"title":"Conforms To","kind":"relationships","type":"conformsTo"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"final","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MultipleElevationCompositeRawToken","kind":"identifier"}],"platforms":["macOS"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"level":2,"anchor":"overview","type":"heading","text":"Overview"},{"code":["        \/\/ Assuming in Figma with have a elevation semantic token none,","        \/\/ with values depending to color scheme. These values are defined as elevation raw tokens.","        let bottom_0 = ElevationCompositeRawToken(x: x0, y: y0, blur: blur0, color: ColorRawTokens.opacityBlack0)","        let bottom_1_100 = ElevationCompositeRawToken(x: x0, y: y100, blur: blur200, color: ColorRawTokens.opacityBlack100)","","        \/\/ Then the development team declares a higher-level elevation semantic token","        \/\/ inside ElevationCompositeSemanticTokens protocol,","        \/\/ and defined inside OrangeTheme+ElevationCompositeSemanticTokens extension","        \/\/ ElevationCompositeSemanticToken is a typealias for MultipleElevationCompositeRawToken to keep same grammar as design kit","        var none: ElevationCompositeSemanticToken {","            ElevationCompositeSemanticToken(light: bottom_0, dark: bottom_1_100)","        }","","        \/\/ If the same elevation is used whatever the color scheme is","        var none: ElevationCompositeSemanticToken {","            ElevationCompositeSemanticToken(bottom_0)","        }"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"code":["        \/\/ The theme exposes both generated elevation semantic tokens and \"crafted\" higher level elevation semantic tokens.","        \/\/ It is recommended to use the higher level version as it is less error-prone.","","        @Environment(\\.theme) var theme","        @Environment(\\.colorScheme) var colorScheme","","        \/\/ Given you want to apply the elevation token \"raised\"","        var body: some View {","            \/\/ Apply the token of elevation for the shadow effect without managing yourself the color scheme","            Rectangle()","                .shadow(elevation: theme.elevations.raised))","        }"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"code":["    \/\/ Or get the token depending to the color scheme and do whatever you want with","    theme.elevations.raised.elevation(for: colorScheme)"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The case of this "},{"code":"MultipleElevationCompositeRawToken","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is quite particular because in fact it contains "},{"code":"MultipleElevationCompositeRawToken","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" (i.e. raw tokens) instead of semantic tokens."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"In fact only the "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"color"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":" of the elevation effect vary depending to the color scheme,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"but in the "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Figma"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":" kit these composite raw tokens are defined for light and dark modes as a single token."}]},{"style":"note","name":"Since","type":"aside","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"0.8.0"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"kind":"content"}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/oudstokenssemantic\/multipleelevationcompositerawtoken"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Semantic tokens which will wrap a combination of "},{"code":"ElevationCompositeRawToken","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" depending to color scheme (i.e. light mode or dark mode)"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Kind of composite token with multiple values, but not named “composite” because this word is already used in the design system."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Allows to gather the multiple-value tokens from "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Figma"}]},{"type":"text","text":" inside one object."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"If an elevation token exists with its value depending to the color scheme, it must be packed in such ``MultipleElevationCompositeRawToken`"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/OUDSTokensSemantic\/documentation\/OUDSTokensSemantic"]]},"references":{"doc://OUDSTokensSemantic/documentation/OUDSTokensSemantic/MultipleElevationCompositeRawToken/elevation(for:)":{"type":"topic","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"elevation"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"for"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:7SwiftUI11ColorSchemeO","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"ColorScheme"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"preciseIdentifier":"c:@M@OUDSTokensRaw@objc(cs)ElevationCompositeRawToken","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"ElevationCompositeRawToken"}],"abstract":[{"text":"Returns the right elevation according to the ","type":"text"},{"code":"colorScheme","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","title":"elevation(for:)","identifier":"doc:\/\/OUDSTokensSemantic\/documentation\/OUDSTokensSemantic\/MultipleElevationCompositeRawToken\/elevation(for:)","url":"\/documentation\/oudstokenssemantic\/multipleelevationcompositerawtoken\/elevation(for:)"},"doc://OUDSTokensSemantic/s16SendableMetatypeP":{"title":"Swift.SendableMetatype","type":"unresolvable","identifier":"doc:\/\/OUDSTokensSemantic\/s16SendableMetatypeP"},"doc://OUDSTokensSemantic/documentation/OUDSTokensSemantic/MultipleElevationCompositeRawToken/light":{"role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/oudstokenssemantic\/multipleelevationcompositerawtoken\/light","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"For "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"light"}]},{"type":"text","text":" mode scheme"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/OUDSTokensSemantic\/documentation\/OUDSTokensSemantic\/MultipleElevationCompositeRawToken\/light","type":"topic","title":"light","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"light"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"c:@M@OUDSTokensRaw@objc(cs)ElevationCompositeRawToken","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"ElevationCompositeRawToken"}],"kind":"symbol"},"doc://OUDSTokensSemantic/documentation/OUDSTokensSemantic/MultipleElevationCompositeRawToken/init(light:dark:)":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/OUDSTokensSemantic\/documentation\/OUDSTokensSemantic\/MultipleElevationCompositeRawToken\/init(light:dark:)","url":"\/documentation\/oudstokenssemantic\/multipleelevationcompositerawtoken\/init(light:dark:)","kind":"symbol","title":"init(light:dark:)","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"init","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"light","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"prec